exit=0
--- stdout ---
Host lifecycle commands, dispatched to the appliance backend installed
with the product. These run host-locally: they do not need the gateway API
and keep working while the gateway container is stopped or unhealthy.

Usage:
  loxicmd appliance [flags]
  loxicmd appliance [command]

Available Commands:
  backup         Encrypted appliance backups
  credentials    Initial appliance credentials
  diagnostics    Appliance support diagnostics
  factory-reset  Not available in this release
  gateway        Local gateway registration in OAM
  logs           Retrieve bounded, redacted logs for an approved component
  network        Appliance network checks (read-only)
  public-address Appliance public address (CSP 1:1 NAT) management
  restore        Not available in this release
  rollback       Not available in this release
  status         Read the complete appliance lifecycle state (read-only)
  update         Not available in this release

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for appliance

Global Flags:
  -s, --apiserver string   Set API server IP address (default "127.0.0.1")
      --bearer             Send the token as 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' (required by the inference gateway; disable for classic loxilb raw-token targets) (default true)
      --cacert string      CA certificate (PEM) to verify the server (https only)
      --cert string        Client certificate (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -k, --insecure           Skip TLS certificate verification (https only)
      --key string         Client private key (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -o, --output string      Set output layer (ex.) wide, json)
  -p, --port int           Set API server port number (default 11111)
      --protocol string    Set API server http/https (default "http")
  -t, --timeout int16      Set timeout (default 10)
      --token string       Set Token for the API server

Use "loxicmd appliance [command] --help" for more information about a command.
